                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>The Laboratory Course in Pharmaceutical Analysis serves as a core practical program that bridges theoretical knowledge in pharmaceutical analysis with real-world applications in drug quality control. Building upon the theoretical curriculum, this course systematically integrates fundamental principles and experimental techniques of pharmaceutical analysis through a 36-class program divided into 9 thematic laboratory sessions. It aims to equip students with critical competencies in pharmaceutical quality analysis and analytical method validation. The curriculum covers essential techniques such as volumetric analysis, spectrophotometry, and chromatography, while aligning all experimental designs with both Chinese and international pharmaceutical standards. By engaging in hands-on experiments, students deepen their understanding of theoretical concepts, refine their technical skills, and broaden their international perspective on global quality control practices.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
